# Allowlist for scripts/check-stale-candidate-refs.sh.
#
# The current candidate is v0.10.0-rc.11. References to the superseded
# v0.10.0-rc.8, v0.10.0-rc.9 and v0.10.0-rc.10 candidates (pattern:
# rc\.8|20cc13a|rc\.9|07d2ba2|rc\.10|0745957) are allowed only in the
# historical records below. Prefer section rules for historical sections over
# line rules. Rule syntax is documented in the script header.

# Historical identity record for rc.8 (later candidates are recorded on their
# certification branches).
file docs/releases/v0.10-candidate-identity-reconciliation.md
# Per-candidate release notes are point-in-time records.
file docs/releases/v0.10.0-rc.*.md
# Archived notes are historical by definition (AGENTS.md).
file docs/archive/*

# VERSION_HISTORY history sections.
section docs/releases/VERSION_HISTORY.md ### v0.10.0-rc.8 — Divergent stabilization candidate (superseded)
section docs/releases/VERSION_HISTORY.md ### v0.10.0-rc.9 — Worker idempotency and attribution fixes (superseded)
section docs/releases/VERSION_HISTORY.md ### v0.10.0-rc.10 — Approval finalization fix (superseded)

# Certification record: the rc.10, rc.9 and rc.8 identities kept as history
# below the rc.11 record, the invalidated rc.10 run, and the findings table,
# whose rows are point-in-time defect records (FIND-011 to FIND-018 cite the
# rc.10 tag).
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Historical rc.10 candidate identity (superseded)
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Historical rc.9 candidate identity (superseded)
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Historical rc.8 candidate identity (superseded)
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Invalidated certification runs
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Findings

# Lines that explicitly label the reference as superseded, historical, or
# invalidated.
line superseded|historical|invalidated

# The approval finalization defect range (rc.1 through rc.9), as written in the
# remediation runbook and the rc.10 notes: "rc.1 through rc.9", "rc.1-rc.9",
# "rc.1–rc.9", "`v0.10.0-rc.1` through `v0.10.0-rc.9`".
line rc\.1`?( through | to |-|–)`?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.9

# Behaviour attributed to the rc.9 change set, which later candidates keep
# ("since rc.9", "before rc.9", "fixed in rc.9", "resolved in `v0.10.0-rc.9`").
line (since|before|fixed in|resolved in|changed in) `?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.9

# Behaviour attributed to the rc.10 change set or to releases up to it ("first
# shipped in `v0.10.0-rc.10`", "releases up to v0.10.0-rc.10", "`v0.10.0-rc.10`
# (or earlier)").
line (first shipped in|up to) `?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.10
line rc\.10`? \(or earlier\)

# rc.11 lineage and proof wording: "rc.10 tag plus the rc.11 fix commits",
# "a test that fails at the rc.10 tag".
line rc\.10 tag plus the rc\.11
line fails? at (the )?`?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.10`? tag

# The rc.10 forensic dump of the pre-rebuild staging database, kept under the
# rc.10 evidence prefix ("v0.10.0-rc.10/forensics/", "the rc.10 forensic dump").
line rc\.10(/forensics| forensic)
